    "forward_axis": "+X",
    "left_axis": "+Y",
    "up_axis": "+Z",
    "positive_pitch": "Right-hand rotation about +Y; body COM moves toward +X for positive pitch deviation.",
    "positive_wheel_effort": "Both wheel joints rotate about +Y; positive equal wheel effort drives forward +X under no-slip rolling.",
    "state_pitch": "theta = atan2(body_COM_world.x - axle_world.x, body_COM_world.z - axle_world.z), in the sagittal plane at zero yaw. Base pitch alone needs the equilibrium offset.",
    "input": "tau is TOTAL torque on both wheels; apply +tau/2 to each wheel joint. The reaction on the nonwheel body is -tau.",
    "generalized_force": "For q=[axle_x, COM_pitch], Q=[tau/radius, -tau]; include both entries."
  },
  "assumptions": [
    "The six nonwheel actuated joints are held at zero angles. The nonwheel body includes base, both abad/hip/knee links, and the fixed IMU.",
    "The rigid-body sagittal approximation ignores leg deflection, yaw/roll, slip, and the small transverse COM offset.",
    "Body inertia is the nonwheel aggregate inertia ABOUT ITS COM, projected on base +Y. It excludes the body_mass*length^2 parallel-axis term.",
    "length is hypot(COM_from_axle.x, COM_from_axle.z); body COM is aligned vertically above the axle at equilibrium_base_pitch_rad.",
    "Wheel inertia is the sum about each physical wheel's rolling axis through its joint origin, including the tiny x/z COM-offset parallel-axis terms.",
    "Wheel COM radial offsets of 30 micrometers and -20 micrometers are ignored in equilibrium/rolling kinematics; the inertial correction remains included.",
    "All inertia tensors are evaluated by rotating USD principal-axis diagonal inertia into base axes, then applying the parallel-axis theorem.",
    "The nominal rolling radius is the collision Cylinder radius, not the slightly larger visual mesh radius. The cylinder height is its axial width.",
    "No contact/rest offset is authored on the upstream collision groups. The configured runtime may use defaults; rest offset, ground rest offset, cylinder approximation, and penetration can change the effective axle height.",
    "The upstream CollisionAPI is on each link/collisions Xform. Geometric Cylinder descendants do not themselves carry the API. Verify runtime collision parsing; if unsupported, apply collision APIs to those existing collision geometries in the scene override.",
    "PD stiffness500/damping30 and other controller settings are supplied by the runtime; these are not part of the asset-derived parameters."
  ],
  "aggregation_formula": {
    "com": "C = sum(m_i * C_i) / sum(m_i)",
    "inertia": "I_C = sum(R_i * diag(Iprincipal_i) * transpose(R_i) + m_i * (dot(d_i,d_i)*Identity - outer(d_i,d_i))), d_i=C_i-C",
    "equilibrium_pitch": "-atan2(body_com_from_axle[0], body_com_from_axle[2])"
  },
